  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>a00fc4df248d930abd79541a41ffabb2</srcmd5>
    <version>0.1.15</version>
    <time>1790585185</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update python-kornia-rs to 0.1.15.

The notable packaging change is the source. Upstream removed --sdist from
its release workflow in 0.1.15 (&quot;not self-contained&quot;), so no PyPI sdist
exists for this or any later version; Source0 therefore points at the
v0.1.15 release tag. Two consequences: the unpacked tree is
kornia-rs-0.1.15 rather than kornia_rs-0.1.15, and pyproject.toml now
lives in the binding crate rather than at the top level, so the PEP 517
build is wrapped in &quot;pushd kornia-py&quot;.

The vendored registry grows from 88 MB to 269 MB because the tag's
workspace also carries examples/* and kornia-cpp, which the generated
sdist pruned; only the kornia-py closure is ever compiled.
BuildRequires: rust moves to &gt;= 1.89, upstream's new rust-version.

Licence re-audited against the new vendor tree (163 crates, no
copyleft), so License: is unchanged.

Native aarch64 build green, %check 18 passed per flavour, rpmlint
0 errors / 0 badness (the two unstripped-.so warnings are pre-existing
and identical in the shipped 0.1.14 build).

Upstream names no CVE or GHSA across the 400 commits crossed, and no
Bugzilla report references the package.
</comment>
    <requestid>1380837</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>14bc78738fc4bc381f142dff12928f87</srcmd5>
